 presented. The 39-year-old woman had spread a warfarin-type rat poison around her house weekly using her bare hands, with no washing post application. Percutaneous absorption of warfarin causing coagulopathy, reported three times in the past, is a significant risk if protective measures, such as gloves, are not used. An adverse drug interaction with piroxicam, which she took occasionally, may have exacerbated the coagulopathy.","metrics":{"precision":0.16666666666666666,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.2857142857142857,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":5,"rel_fn":0}}